<title>SPAIN: Amper says to pay 40 ptas gross interim dividend.</title>
<headline>Amper says to pay 40 ptas gross interim dividend.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish telecommunications equipment firm Amper said on Wednesday it will pay an interim dividend of 40 pesetas gross, effective December 26.</p>
<p>In a meeting the firm's board also named Juan Perea chairman. Perea is former director general for planning at Telefonica.</p>
<p>Telefonica is Amper's majority shareholder, with around a 15 percent stake.</p>
<p>Amper has not paid dividends since 1990.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
